course: dictionary
lesson: 7094
title: Peaceful: calm, or without fighting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Peaceful has two main meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Read the words around it. «The lake was peaceful at dawn, with no wind and no sound.» Here peaceful means calm and quiet, without noise or worry.
explain: The word can also mean without war or fighting. «Suffragists campaigned for votes for women with petitions, meetings and peaceful marches.» The clues are petitions and meetings: the campaigners did not use violence, so peaceful means without violence.
explain: Ask yourself: is this about a quiet place or mood, or about how people behaved? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Peaceful means calm and quiet, without noise or worry, as in «a peaceful place».
fact: Peaceful also means without war or fighting, so a peaceful protest does not use violence.
fact: Peaceful is an adjective, so it can change: peaceful, more peaceful, most peaceful.
fact: «He found an ocean so calm that he named it the Pacific, meaning peaceful.»
fact: In a gentle way of talking about death, people say someone «died peacefully».
exercise: «After the conquests the Mongol lands were peaceful enough for traders to travel safely across Asia.» What does peaceful mean here? | Happy and loud | Covered in snow | Very noisy and busy | *Without war or fighting
exercise: «Good rules protect people; unfair rules can be changed by fair and peaceful means.» What does peaceful mean here? | Happy and laughing | *Without violence | Very quiet, with no one speaking | Very fast and sudden
exercise: «He found a stormy passage, then came out onto an ocean so calm that he named it the Pacific.» Find and copy one word that means calm. | named | stormy | passage | *calm
test: «The village was peaceful, and the children played by the river all afternoon.» What does peaceful mean here? | Covered in war | *Calm and quiet, without noise or worry | Very fast | Angry and crowded
test: Priya says peaceful and quiet always mean the same thing. Why is she wrong? | Quiet is a longer word | Peaceful is only used about the sea | *Peaceful can mean without war, and quiet does not | She is right, they always mean the same
exam: Which sentence uses peaceful to mean without violence? | *Suffragists held peaceful marches for votes for women | Rain fell on the peaceful lake | The peaceful dog slept by the fire | Her peaceful bedroom was painted blue
